    "finding": {
      "what": "iOS delivered UIKit's memory warning and Kit's dispatch source at the same moment, as critical with no warning first. The idle model released within 60 ms. But iOS never reported a return to normal: after the ballast was freed, Kit still read critical for 60 s and refused a load, and kern.memorystatus_vm_pressure_level can't be read from the app (-1).",
      "run": {
        "build": "3639590 (critical lifted only by a normal notice)",
        "dispatchLevelsSeen": [
          "normal",
          "critical"
        ],
        "thirdReply": "refused: insufficientMemory after 60 s"
      },
      "fix": "User decision 2026-10-29: critical eases on a normal notice, once the app's available memory has recovered to twice what it was at the notice, or 60 s after the last critical notice. The final run above shows it easing on recovery and the third reply loading."
    },
